< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/looper/issues/122#issuecomment-6845470950 Blocked-by: #128
The fix for #122 is done and queued to land, but it isn't on main. The build system has given no result for any of this repository's lands since 2026-11-11, so I've marked the issue blocked on #128.

**The fix:** commit 67eb715 changes only `tests/repo-looper.test.sh`. It's the previous run's fix moved onto the current main, unchanged.
- The test's manager now waits until each report has started work before it can end. That removes the race that hung the gates for 48 minutes.
- Every `repo-looper` the test runs is stopped after 300 seconds. A wait that never ends now fails its scenario instead of hanging.
- A new scenario, `slow-start`, makes a report start later than the manager's 5-second linger. The manager still merges its land.

**Local test:** `tests/repo-looper.test.sh` passed: 143 `ok`, all scenarios pass, 14m45s. One scenario only runs as root, so it was skipped here and its part of the change is not checked locally.

**Why it isn't landed:** the last land went red with "no verdict within 3h", and the earlier build check ended the same way. Every land in this repository has failed like that since 2026-11-11 (#101, #104, #108, #112, #113). The cause is #128: the build queue is backed up, and the manager counts a build that hasn't started yet as a failure. I could not open the build pipelines myself (access returns 404), so that cause comes from #128's reports.

**What I did:**
- Queued the land again at 05:57Z. It runs the full gates, because this test file maps to the full set.
- Posted a status comment on the issue.
- Wrote `Blocked-by: #128` as the run's outcome.

The issue stays open. Once #128 is closed, the next run checks this land's result, posts the final comment and closes #122.
